From 42723f0df2af39d19fa4e5b4bd6e977d21ee781d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:36:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_vacancy_growth_cap, v2_vacancy_chart_split,
 v2_rookie_backup_wr_dampen (broad) and v2_cold_start_room_budget

Cold-start receiver guards, all backtested on week 1 2022-2025 and rejected:
- v2_cold_start_room_budget: ALL +0.019*, WR +0.047*, START-WR +0.077* (it water-filled real WR1s such as 2025 NE Diggs to the floor).
- v2_rookie_backup_wr_dampen (broad): ALL +0.009, WR +0.013, TE +0.018*; no strength helped; it docked a boom/modest-role pool
  (2023 Puka Nacua). The narrow version (shipped) keeps ROOKIE_BACKUP_WR_SHARE and the _STRENGTH dial.
- v2_vacancy_growth_cap: ALL -0.007, TE -0.042*, startables CI spans 0, similar to the bump cap that shipped.
- v2_vacancy_chart_split: weak alone; stacked with bump + growth it made START-TE +0.206* (significant) - not to be combined.
apply_cold_start_receiver_vacancy keeps only the shipped max_bump guard; prior_room_snap_budget / apply_cold_start_room_snap_budget,
the growth-cap and chart-rank constants, three sweep scripts and the tests of the removed behavior are gone. Default cold-start
boards identical (.sweeps/board_identity.py: 2022 w1, 2024 w1, live 2026 w1, 2025 w1 with the Ourlads charts).
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
